title: Linux and macOS builds and build documentation
---
date: 2026-04-15
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: TitleFlow gained distributable Linux and macOS binaries and a BUILD guide covering all three platforms.
---
tags: release, documentation
---
source_commit: 8fc014e4934b4c5337ae9378fe6b8bcbaa6a6648
---
body:

The second commit in the repository made TitleFlow easier to run on other
systems. It added prebuilt binaries for Linux on x86-64 and for macOS on both
Intel and Apple Silicon, kept under `build/`, and a `BUILD.md` that explains the
process.

Because TitleFlow is a single stateless Go program, building for another
platform is a matter of setting `GOOS` and `GOARCH`. The guide lists the
three targets and states the only prerequisite: Go 1.26 or newer. The ignore
rules were updated to exclude local build artifacts such as `.exe` files while
keeping the distributable binaries in `build/`.

[Commit 8fc014e](https://github.com/Labyricorn/TitleFlow/commit/8fc014e4934b4c5337ae9378fe6b8bcbaa6a6648)
